# Frontend

Next.js 16 App Router. Before a new framework API, read the matching page in `apps/frontend/node_modules/next/dist/docs/`.

- `src/app` is routes only: `layout.tsx`, `globals.css`, and a thin `page.tsx` per path
- Feature UI lives in `src/features/shell`, `console`, `watcher`, and `reports`. A feature does not import another feature
- Shared HTTP, socket, and formatting live in `src/lib`. Domain types come from `@saf-shekan/core`
- Interactive controls use `@/components/ui`. Do not use a raw `select`, `button`, `input`, or `dialog` when that primitive exists
- The browser calls the Nest API only (`/api`, `/ws`). No broker or TSETMC HTTP from the client
- Visual source is the Stitch terminal (dark canvas, Yekan/Vazirmatn text, JetBrains Mono numbers). Do not port ZARVA layouts
